==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|ƿite}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*wītiją|t=punishment}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|wīte}}, {{cog|osx|wīti}}, {{cog|nl|wijte}}, {{cog|goh|wīzi}},  {{cog|non|víti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈwiːte/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=wīte|n|wītu}}

# [[punishment]], [[torment]], [[torture]]
#: ''Hé '''ƿíte''' ƿealdeþ. &mdash; He is the disposer of punishment. (He wields punishment.)''
# [[plague]], [[disease]], [[evil]], [[injury]], [[pain]]
#: ''Of ðam '''ƿíte''' gehǽled;'' &mdash; Healed of the disease.
# [[penalty]], [[fine]], [[bote]]: contribution, in money or food, to sustenance of king or his officers
# [[woe]], [[misery]], [[distress]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-ja-n|wit}}

